Janis Papanagnou wrote:

> You can't disable firetraps.

You can dig down on fire trap and change it into a pit. This will 
disable the firetrap. This is also possible on other traps that cannot 
be untrapped[1].

And before you ask:

Yes, this works for falling rock traps. The reason is that there can 
only be one trap per location so the pit replaces the trap on the 
ceiling. You can rationalize this by saying that digging the pit 
disables the trigger mechanism for the falling rock trap.

[1] Except of course for (spiked) pits, trapdoors and holes, but all 
these can be disabled by pushing a boulder in.

